{"name":"School Bus","hex":"#ffd800","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"school bus","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bus which carries children to or from school.","An informal approximate unit of measure, from the length of a typical public school bus, approximately 30 feet or 9 metres."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/school_bus"}],"entries":[{"title":"School bus","blocks":[{"text":"A school bus is any type of bus owned, leased, contracted to, or operated by a school or school district. It is regularly used to transport students to and from school or school-related activities, but not including a charter bus or transit bus. Various configurations of school buses are used worldwide; the most iconic examples are the yellow school buses of the United States which are also found in other parts of the world, including Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/IC_CE_school_bus_%28shortened_chassis%29.jpg/330px-IC_CE_school_bus_%28shortened_chassis%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School_bus","wikidata":"Q58678"},{"title":"School Bus (film)","blocks":[{"text":"School Bus is a 2016 Indian Malayalam-language thriller film directed by Rosshan Andrrews. The film stars Kunchacko Boban, Jayasurya, and Aparna Gopinath in the lead roles. The screenplay is written by Bobby–Sanjay."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/77/School_Bus_%282016%29_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School_Bus_(film)","wikidata":"Q23647148"},{"title":"School","blocks":[{"text":"A school is an educational institution designed to provide learning environments for the teaching of students, usually under the direction of teachers. Most countries have systems of formal education, which is sometimes compulsory. In these systems, students progress through a series of schools that can be built and operated by both government and private organizations. The names for these schools vary by country but generally include primary school for young children and secondary school for teenagers who have completed primary education. An institution where higher education is taught is commonly called a university college or university."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/%D0%A8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0_%E2%84%962_%D0%B3._%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D1%8C%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg/330px-%D0%A8%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%BB%D0%B0_%E2%84%962_%D0%B3._%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%81%D0%BD%D0%BE%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D1%8C%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/School","wikidata":"Q3914"},{"title":"Bus","blocks":[{"text":"A bus is a motor vehicle that carries significantly more passengers than an average car or van, but fewer than the average rail transport. It is most commonly used in public transport, but is also in use for charter purposes, or through private ownership. Although buses typically carry between 30 and 100 passengers, some buses have a capacity of up to 300 passengers. The most common type is the single-deck rigid bus, with double-decker and articulated buses carrying larger loads, and midibuses and minibuses carrying smaller loads. Coaches are used for longer-distance services. Many types of buses, such as city transit buses and inter-city coaches, charge a fare. Other types, such as elementary or secondary school buses or shuttle buses within a post-secondary education campus, are free. In many jurisdictions, bus drivers require a special large vehicle licence above and beyond a regular driving license."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/LTZ1328-19-20241030-160332.jpg/330px-LTZ1328-19-20241030-160332.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bus","wikidata":"Q5638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg/500px-2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg/1280px-2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg/500px-2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2010_Thomas_Saf-T-Liner_C2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Thomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg/500px-Thomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Thomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg/1280px-Thomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Thomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg/500px-Thomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThomas_C2_interior_seats.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Country_District_School_Wagon.jpg/500px-Country_District_School_Wagon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Country_District_School_Wagon.jpg/500px-Country_District_School_Wagon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One-horse kid hack (Early 1910s)","link":"https://en.wi